{{also|Then}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|den||AAVE|Bermuda|}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|[[then]]([[thenne|ne]])}}, {{m|enm|[[than]]([[thanne|ne]])}}, from {{inh|en|ang|þonne}}, {{m|ang|þanne}}, {{m|ang|þænne||then, at that time}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*þan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*þan||at that (time), then}}, from earlier {{m|gem-pro||*þam}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*tóm}}, accusative masculine of {{m|ine-pro|*só||demonstrative pronoun, that}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|nl|dan||then}}, {{cog|de|dann||then}}, {{cog|is|þá||then}}. Doublet of {{l|en|than}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ðɛn/|a=UK,US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ðen/|a=Australia}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-then.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛn|s=1}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|temporal location}} At that [[time]].
#: {{ux|en|He was happy '''then'''.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Genesis|12|6|passage=And the Canaanite was '''then''' in the land.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=1|passage=In the old days, to my commonplace and unobserving mind, he gave no evidences of genius whatsoever. He never read me any of his manuscripts,&nbsp;[&hellip;], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned. But he had '''then''' none of the oddities and mannerisms which I hold to be inseparable from genius, and which struck my attention in after days when I came in contact with the Celebrity.}}
# {{lb|en|temporal location}} Soon afterward.
#: {{ux|en|He fixed it, '''then''' left.}}
#: {{ux|en|Turn left, '''then''' right, '''then''' right again, '''then''' keep going until you reach the service station.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Matthew|5|24|passage=First be reconciled to thy brother, and '''then''' come and offer thy gift.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=1|passage='''Then''' there came a reg'lar terror of a sou'wester same as you don't get one summer in a thousand, and blowed the shanty flat and ripped about half of the weir poles out of the sand. We spent consider'ble money getting 'em reset, and '''then''' a swordfish got into the pound and tore the nets all to slathers, right in the middle of the squiteague season.}}
# {{lb|en|sequence}} Next in order of place.
#: {{ux|en|There are three green ones, '''then''' a blue one.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=5|passage='''Then''' came a maid with hand-bag and shawls, and after her a tall young lady. She stood for a moment holding her skirt above the grimy steps, with something of the stately pose which Richter has given his Queen Louise on the stairway, and the light of the reflector fell full upon her.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-19|author=w:Peter Wilby
|volume=189|issue=6|page=30|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=[http://www.theguardian.com/education/2013/jul/01/education-michael-gove-finland-gcse Finland spreads word on schools]
|passage=Imagine a country where children do nothing but play until they start compulsory schooling at age seven. '''Then''', without exception, they attend comprehensives until the age of 16. Charging school fees is illegal, and so is sorting pupils into ability groups by streaming or setting.}}
# [[in addition|In addition]]; [[also]]; [[besides]].
#* {{quote-book|en|chapter=[[s:Peeps at Many Lands: Siam/Chapter 17|Chapter 17 White elephants]]|title=Peeps at Many Lands: Siam|author=E Young|year=1908|publisher=Adam and Charles Black|location=London|page=75|text=Another legend says that now and again in the world's history a monarch appears who conquers and rules every nation under the sun. {{...}} '''Then''' many of the Siamese believe that the animal is inhabited by the soul of some great man of the past {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|conjunctive}} In that case.
#: {{ux|en|If it’s locked, '''then''' we’ll need the key.}}
#: {{ux|en|Is it 12 o'clock already? '''Then''' it's time for me to leave.}}
#: {{ux|en|You don't like potatoes? What do you want me to cook, '''then'''?}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1859|title=[[w:Rubaiyat of Omar Khayyam|The Rub&aacute;iy&aacute;t of Omar Khayy&aacute;m: The Astronomer-Poet of Persia]]|author=w:Edward Fitzgerald|page=1|text=And, as the Cock crew, those who stood before<br>The Tavern shouted — "Open '''then''' the Door!<br>You know how little while we have to stay,<br>And, once departed, may return no more."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1749|title=The Universal Magazine|volume=4|page=321
|passage=That happy minute would elate me, / End all my sorrow, grief, and cares; / '''Then''' do not frown, altho' you hate me, / But smile and dissipate my fears: {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|sequence}} [[at the same time|At the same time]]; [[on the other hand]].
#: {{ux|en|That’s a nice shirt, but '''then''', so is the other one.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|dialect|affirmation}} Used to contradict an assertion.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2001|author=w:Eric Malpass|title=At the Height of the Moon|page=28|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=cClq1igzauQC&pg=PA28&dq=%22She+says+Indian+elephants+are+tidgy+little+things%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=9gsPT9qlMYeaiQf4kdwu&ved=0CDIQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=%22She%20says%20Indian%20elephants%20are%20tidgy%20little%20things%22&f=false|passage=‘She says Indian elephants are tidgy little things.’ <br> ‘They're not '''then'''.’ Emma was getting heated. ‘They're –’ <br> ‘Emma!’ said Jenny sharply. The child subsided.}}

